WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.325
A custom bracelet usually starts as a dozen chat messages.

2
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:09.303
BeadCraft Studio turns that into a storefront, in English and French.

3
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:14.367
Shoppers pick a bead and place it slot by slot, then a cord and a charm.

4
00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:16.969
The price updates with every choice.

5
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:20.971
A finished design gets a link that opens on any phone.

6
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:26.123
Checkout makes it a job on the maker's dashboard, tracked through five stages.

7
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.304
The hard part is trust in the numbers.

8
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:33.469
One pure function adds beads, cord, charm and labour.

9
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:38.075
The browser runs it for the estimate, the server for the final total.

10
00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:43.052
Checkout carries a key, so a retried request returns the same order.

11
00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:48.521
Status changes check the order's version, so two makers can't overwrite each other.

12
00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:52.728
It's live today, built by Hamza Benarfa in Tunis.

